   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Variety: \u2018Abacus\u2019. See fig. 5 in colour section.\nApplication No. 91/092\nApplication Received: 25 November 1991\nApplicant: Luminis Pty. Ltd., The University of Adelaide,\nSouth Australia",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    51.6,
    716.16,
    287.76,
    771.36
   ],
   "id": "e14",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      52.56,
      716.16,
      228.48,
      725.28
     ],
     "text": "Description\u2014see also comparison tables"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      51.84,
      730.08,
      287.28,
      739.2
     ],
     "text": "This variety is a late-maturing, spring type, hexaploid triticale."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      52.8,
      741.12,
      287.52,
      750.0
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Abacus\u2019 has brown chaff, long tapering heads, strongly pig-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      52.08,
      751.92,
      287.52,
      761.04
     ],
     "text": "mented flag leaf auricles and pubescence present on the pedun-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      51.6,
      762.72,
      287.76,
      771.36
     ],
     "text": "cle. \u2018Abacus\u2019 has a longer head than \u2018Muir\u2019 or \u2018Tahara\u2019 and a"
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Description\u2014see also comparison tables\nThis variety is a late-maturing, spring type, hexaploid triticale.\n\u2018Abacus\u2019 has brown chaff, long tapering heads, strongly pig-\nmented flag leaf auricles and pubescence present on the pedun-\ncle. \u2018Abacus\u2019 has a longer head than \u2018Muir\u2019 or \u2018Tahara\u2019 and a",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    315.36,
    607.68,
    551.52,
    770.64
   ],
   "id": "e15",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      316.08,
      607.68,
      551.52,
      616.8
     ],
     "text": "denser head with shorter awns than \u2018Currency\u2019. Unlike"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      316.8,
      618.24,
      551.28,
      627.6
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Currency\u2019 but like \u2018Muir\u2019 and \u2018Tahara\u2019, \u2018Abacus\u2019 has good"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.84,
      629.04,
      551.04,
      637.92
     ],
     "text": "resistance to Puccinia graminis ssp. tritici race 34\u20142, 12, 13."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.84,
      648.24,
      342.72,
      657.12
     ],
     "text": "Origin"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      662.64,
      551.28,
      672.0
     ],
     "text": "The breeder is K V Cooper of the University of Adelaide, South"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.84,
      673.44,
      551.04,
      683.04
     ],
     "text": "Australia. \u2018Abacus\u2019 derives from a locally produced primary"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.84,
      684.48,
      551.04,
      694.08
     ],
     "text": "triticale topcrossed to advanced triticale varieties. The pedigree"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      695.52,
      550.8,
      705.12
     ],
     "text": "of \u2018Abacus\u2019 is K875/\u2018Snoopy\u2019//T2893/3/ \u2018Currency\u2019. K875"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.6,
      706.8,
      551.04,
      715.92
     ],
     "text": "(bread wheat), \u2018Anza\u2019/\u2018Raven\u2019//\u2018Olympic\u2019/Siete Cerros 66"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      717.6,
      550.8,
      727.2
     ],
     "text": "obtained from A.J. Rathjen was crossed with \u2018Snoopy\u2019 Rye,"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      728.64,
      551.04,
      738.0
     ],
     "text": "and amphiploids were obtained by embryo culture and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      739.44,
      550.8,
      748.8
     ],
     "text": "colchicine treatment. The resulting primary triticale was"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.6,
      750.72,
      551.28,
      759.84
     ],
     "text": "topcrossed with T2898(BGL\u201ds\u201d/ARS\u2014Mexipak Mut //"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      761.28,
      550.08,
      770.64
     ],
     "text": "BGL\u201ds\u201d, entry 192 in 10th ITSN) and \u2018Currency\u2019. \u2018Abacus\u2019"
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "denser head with shorter awns than \u2018Currency\u2019. Unlike\n\u2018Currency\u2019 but like \u2018Muir\u2019 and \u2018Tahara\u2019, \u2018Abacus\u2019 has good\nresistance to Puccinia graminis ssp. tritici race 34\u20142, 12, 13.\nOrigin\nThe breeder is K V Cooper of the University of Adelaide, South\nAustralia. \u2018Abacus\u2019 derives from a locally produced primary\ntriticale topcrossed to advanced triticale varieties. The pedigree\nof \u2018Abacus\u2019 is K875/\u2018Snoopy\u2019//T2893/3/ \u2018Currency\u2019. K875\n(bread wheat), \u2018Anza\u2019/\u2018Raven\u2019//\u2018Olympic\u2019/Siete Cerros 66\nobtained from A.J. Rathjen was crossed with \u2018Snoopy\u2019 Rye,\nand amphiploids were obtained by embryo culture and\ncolchicine treatment. The resulting primary triticale was\ntopcrossed with T2898(BGL\u201ds\u201d/ARS\u2014Mexipak Mut //\nBGL\u201ds\u201d, entry 192 in 10th ITSN) and \u2018Currency\u2019. \u2018Abacus\u2019",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
